# Rust build output. CARGO_TARGET_DIR usually points elsewhere (see bin/ci), but a bare
# `cargo build` still writes here.
/target

# >>> repo-harness:gitignore-private-boundary >>>
# Maintainer notes — not part of the project; they live in the private notes repo,
# reachable through the `local` symlink. NO trailing slash on any path in this block:
# a worktree materializes these paths as SYMLINKS, and a `foo/` pattern matches a real
# directory only — the ignore then keeps working in the main tree and silently fails
# in every worktree.
/local

# Environment secrets and the per-machine agent sandbox config. `.env.*` covers the
# variants a real session produces — `.env.local`, and above all the `.env.bak.<epoch>`
# an editor or a script leaves behind. One of those sat untracked in a repo for weeks:
# the pre-commit secret scan only reads what is staged, so a secret nobody stages is a
# secret nobody scans, and `.env` alone does not match it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.ai-jail
# <<< repo-harness:gitignore-private-boundary <<<

# The beads tracker's own directory. Everything in it is machine-local: the SQLite
# database, its WAL and lock files, and the JSONL export beside them. Committing any of
# it would put a binary database and a churn-heavy export into the history for no reader.
# No trailing slash, for the reason the block above spells out: a worktree can
# materialize this as a symlink.
/.beads

# bv (beads viewer) local config and caches
.bv/

# The Agent Mail reservation guard plugin. `guard install` generates it per machine with
# absolute paths baked in (the mailbox store and this project's reservation directory), so
# it is regenerated on each checkout rather than committed. The chain runner beside it
# (`.githooks/pre-commit`) is generic and IS committed, as is the secret-scan hook it
# preserves at `.githooks/pre-commit.orig`.
/.githooks/hooks.d

# ntm's per-project runtime state, written by the swarm tooling when it drives this repository:
# `logs/` and `pids/` for the panes it spawns, and `rate_limits.json` for what it has observed of
# the upstream accounts. All three are facts about one machine at one moment, so committing them
# would put another machine's pane ids and one afternoon's rate-limit counters in every checkout.
/.ntm

# The beads compliance audit's own directory. It is a separate repository with its own
# history (one commit per verification pass) that lives inside this tree so the scorecards
# stay next to the code they cite. Nothing in it belongs in this project's history. No
# trailing slash, for the reason the private-boundary block above spells out.
/beads_compliance_audit
